WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
Two people each find a lost
wallet, stuffed with cash.

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.730
Both hand it straight back to its owner.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:07.670
Same act.

4
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.440
Same happy ending.

5
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:13.580
Yet the philosopher Immanuel
Kant, writing in 1785,

6
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.640
would not rate them equally.

7
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:19.330
So why would Kant say only
one of them acted morally?

8
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.010
In this mission, you'll see why Kant
says a real moral command can never begin

9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.790
with: if you want this, do that.

10
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.830
Then you'll put everyday
rules through Kant's tests,

11
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.110
step by step, and watch
which ones survive.

12
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.490
Your mission: find out why Kant would
judge the two finders differently.
